From d43492b165233d60656784ad6739ac1b7ec95e48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:36:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/49] Eden (Doris): wait briefly for compiling shaders
 instead of hiding the draw

With asynchronous shaders on, Eden drops every draw whose pipeline is still compiling, so new
areas flicker as objects, terrain and shadows pop in. Doris now waits for the pipeline first,
from a budget of doris_async_shader_wait_ms (default 8 ms) shared by all draws in a ~33 ms window;
only if it is still not ready is the draw skipped. 0 restores Eden's behaviour.
Build completion now wakes every waiter (notify_all), since two threads can wait on it.
